From b5e4613c632b47056fba3de6064bc56b00bedcb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:31:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Upload stage: never keep remote response bodies; an unknown
 upload stays unknown (root review)

1) Relay, gateway and storage-fetch failures are reported, journaled and shown only as a
   fixed diagnostic plus at most an HTTP status; an upstream body may reflect the signature
   or token. A gateway CID is kept only if CID-shaped; signature-recovery errors are generic.
   Test: fake relay/gateway reflect signature and token in error bodies and the CID field.
2) verify-storage never resets upload-unknown on a failed fetch (timeout, 5xx, network or
   404 prove nothing); the reason says so. The only way back to an authorization is the
   administrator's explicit same-bytes/same-CID retry; nothing re-uploads by itself.
Tests (queue 512): handoff 12/12, browser 2/2, mutants 21/21. Still inactive.
